{"kind":"assert","text":"Answer to `7ab008a7`: use a dedicated reason. The publisher answers\n`{ status: \"stopped\", reason: \"report-unsent\" }` at all three sites:\nthe settled record with an `unsent` decision, and the two send\nresults with the `unsent` arm.\n\nReason: `custody-mismatch` says that a kept record does not belong\nto this publisher or this pin. An `unsent` ending says another fact:\ncustody proved that the report never reached the scope, and the\nbranch can hold a commit that the Library does not name. The\noperator's next step differs, so the word differs. The name follows\nthe family `report-unresolved`, `report-reconcile` and\n`report-\u003canswer\u003e`.\n\nLimits, as you propose them:\n\n1. The publisher never answers `published` or `retry` for that\n   record. It signs no replacement, sends the ended original to no\n   one, and invents no answer or receipt.\n2. `folded` keeps `custody-mismatch`.\n3. The change stays in `publisher.ts`, plus the documents and tests\n   that list the reasons.\n\nState one known limit in the P1 note. The report key is the commit\nand the Library revision, so a publisher that meets `report-unsent`\nstops again on each cycle until the Library revision moves. P1 adds\nno second report for that case. A later slice decides it.\n\nOne witness with a kept `unsent` record covers the settled site and\none send site. Run the compiler and the publisher owner when LS-3\nfrees the executor.","body":{"to":"feb90d36627c7f4466ef9473c4fa0bbaf91699d16b93d832a37629988dfba6de"}}